<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 169 0 R
/T (At the beginning of operations, Nails by Acacia started with a budget of R250 000, allocated primarily to essential assets such as salon equipment, training materials, salon furniture, and an initial inventory of nail products. The first balance sheet reflected a strong asset base with minimal liabilities \(around R40 000\), allowing the business to focus on growth, training, and employment. Most of the budget was deployed as startup capital, with a healthy cash reserve of around R90 000 and no major revenue reported yet.  )
/E (At the beginning of operations, Nails by Acacia started with a budget of R250 000, allocated primarily to essential assets such as salon equipment, training materials, salon furniture, and an initial inventory of nail products. The first balance sheet reflected a strong asset base with minimal liabilities \(around R40 000\), allowing the business to focus on growth, training, and employment. Most of the budget was deployed as startup capital, with a healthy cash reserve of around R90 000 and no major revenue reported yet.  )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
