730 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 169 0 R
/T (By December 2025, the end-of-year balance sheet reflected significant growth and activity. The salon had generated R500 000 in revenue, with total expenses of R420 000, resulting in a net profit of R80 000. From this profit, 20% \(R16 000\) was paid out as shareholder dividends, while R64 000 was retained in the business to support future growth. The updated balance sheet showed total assets of R254 000, with increased inventory, accounts receivable, and equipment value. Liabilities also increased slightly to R50 000, primarily due to a business loan and accrued operational costs. The equity of the business grew to R204 000, showing strong financial performance, reinvestment, and responsible dividend distribution, which positions the salon for future expansion and stability.  )
/E (By December 2025, the end-of-year balance sheet reflected significant growth and activity. The salon had generated R500 000 in revenue, with total expenses of R420 000, resulting in a net profit of R80 000. From this profit, 20% \(R16 000\) was paid out as shareholder dividends, while R64 000 was retained in the business to support future growth. The updated balance sheet showed total assets of R254 000, with increased inventory, accounts receivable, and equipment value. Liabilities also increased slightly to R50 000, primarily due to a business loan and accrued operational costs. The equity of the business grew to R204 000, showing strong financial performance, reinvestment, and responsible dividend distribution, which positions the salon for future expansion and stability.  )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
